  "final_response": "I fixed `parse_date` in `app/parser.py`, and `tests/test_parser.py::test_dates` now passes.\n\n**The problem:** `split_date` only splits on `-`, so `\"2026/12/31\"` failed with a `ValueError`.\n\n**The fix:** `parse_date` now trims spaces from the input and swaps `/` for `-` before calling `split_date`. I made the change there rather than inside the fallback `split_date`, so dates in either format get the same treatment whichever `split_date` is in use.\n\n**Not checked:** `shared/` isn't in this checkout, so the test only ran against the local fallback version of `split_date`. I couldn't see or run the real `shared.utils.split_date`. If it does more than split on `-`, it's worth re-running the test in a full checkout. No other files were changed.",
